DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       iibbvv__rreegg__mmrr(()) registers a memory region (MR) associated with the protec‐
       tion domain _p_d.  The MR's starting address is  _a_d_d_r  and  its  size  is
       _l_e_n_g_t_h.   The  argument  _a_c_c_e_s_s describes the desired memory protection
       attributes; it is either 0 or the bitwise OR of one or more of the fol‐
       lowing flags:

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__LLOOCCAALL__WWRRIITTEE  Enable Local Write Access

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__RREEMMOOTTEE__WWRRIITTEE  Enable Remote Write Access

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__RREEMMOOTTEE__RREEAADD Enable Remote Read Access

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__RREEMMOOTTEE__AATTOOMMIICC Enable Remote Atomic Operation Access (if sup‐
       ported)

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__MMWW__BBIINNDD Enable Memory Window Binding

       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__OONN__DDEEMMAANNDD Create an on-demand paging MR

       If IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__RREEMMOOTTEE__WWRRIITTEE or  IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__RREEMMOOTTEE__AATTOOMMIICC  is  set,  then
       IIBBVV__AACCCCEESSSS__LLOOCCAALL__WWRRIITTEE must be set too.

       Local read access is always enabled for the MR.

       iibbvv__ddeerreegg__mmrr(()) deregisters the MR _m_r.

