       iibbvv__rreegg__mmrr(()) returns a pointer to the registered MR, or NULL if the re‐
       quest fails.  The local key (LL__KKeeyy) field llkkeeyy  is  used  as  the  lkey
       field of struct ibv_sge when posting buffers with ibv_post_* verbs, and
       the the remote key (RR__KKeeyy) field rrkkeeyy is used by  remote  processes  to
       perform  Atomic  and  RDMA  operations.  The remote process places this
       rrkkeeyy  as  the  rkey  field  of  struct  ibv_send_wr   passed   to   the
       ibv_post_send function.

       iibbvv__ddeerreegg__mmrr(())  returns  0 on success, or the value of errno on failure
